iagnostics.\nXena Githubber\n\n\n### ns__Strategy\n\n(ns__Strategy expanded as its own root — 2 children: each is rendered here or one door away; absence under this node is signal only after its doors.)\n\nchildren (witness depth):\n\n### ns__Decision_DiagnosticFirst\ntype: ns__Decision\nXena: 'Every engagement starts with a diagnostic phase. Never propose solutions before understanding the system.' Two weeks, $5K, 8+ stakeholder interviews.\nDiagnostic First Methodology\nunder: ns__Strategy\n\n### ns__Decision_KnowledgeMapping\ntype: ns__Decision\nVisualize where decisions happen and where knowledge lives. Deliverable: knowledge gap report with prioritized recommendations.\nKnowledge Gap Mapping\nunder: ns__Strategy\n\n\nchildren — expand any (^):\n  sub-themes (2):\n    ^ns__Decision_DiagnosticFirst — Xena: 'Every engagement starts with a diagnostic phase. Never propose solutions before und\n    ^ns__Decision_KnowledgeMapping — Visualize where decisions happen and where knowledge lives. Deliverable: knowledge gap rep\n\n# Doors — ns__Strategy's axes\n\n[ ^ns__Strategy::Thematic — 2 areas ]\nEach door expands to its complete axis, grouped again when it is long.\n\n### ns__Decision_KnowledgeMapping  (already in your context)\n\n### ns__Decision_DiagnosticFirst  (already in your context)\n\n### ns__Actor_XenaGithubber\ntype: ns__Actor\nIndependent consultant specializing in knowledge mapping and organizational diagnostics.\nXena Githubber\n\n\nserved: ^ns__Actor_XenaGithubber, ^ns__Decision_DiagnosticFirst, ^ns__Decision_KnowledgeMapping, ^ns__Strategy\n(pass this list back as `have` on your next expand — content you already hold is then returned as a bare ^pointer, never re-sent)","positions":"","pin":"40e694858454b27ece6bde531ba5d88045adfa91","positions_consult":"{\"positions\":[]}","context_bytes":3956},"live_run_id":"8e52d85aec85","at":"2026-10-01T11:23:37Z"}
